Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: assign the TB522FU keyboard UART alias

The first hardware test reached GNOME but qcom_geni_serial rejected SE15
with "Invalid line -19" before creating a serdev controller. No serial
aliases existed; the pinned driver then used an invalid negative lower
bound for its fallback ID allocation. Give this enabled UART a stable
serial0 alias. Keep the accessory driver manually loaded during bring-up.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -585,3 +585,10 @@
 		pinctrl-2 = <&keyboard_controls &keyboard_wake_off>;
 	};
 };
+
+/* Give the keyboard UART an explicit serial-core line allocation. */
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		serial0 = &uart15;
+	};
+};
